CAOS - Air-Gapped Certificate Authority
=======================================

The root filesystem is read-only.  CA data lives on the encrypted CAOSDATA
partition under /mnt/ca-data and is opened by S10caos-data at boot.

CAOSDATA must be LUKS2-formatted once on first boot; S10caos-data prints the
exact commands if the partition is still empty or unformatted.  The image
itself deliberately contains no LUKS header and no CA private keys.

The CA tools run as the unprivileged "caos" user:
  su -l -s /bin/sh caos
  caos-ca init
  caos-ca issue --cn host.example --san host.example

The S20caos-ca init script performs a startup integrity check with
"caos-ca verify" when the CA has been initialized.  It does not start a
daemon; issue, list, revoke and verify are run manually as described above.

WARNING: this image uses the Buildroot default of an empty root password on
the local console.  Keep the machine physically controlled.  For production,
rebuild with a root password, or apply the console-access controls described
in the project README.
